{
  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_007: multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, None, concat → 53.6% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion is actually contributing value or whether a single modality performs comparably. config_033 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200, None, None) is the cleanest single-variable ablation of config_007: it keeps the same RNA encoder (scvi_n200), same profile setting (singleprofile), and removes only the image modality. If RNA-only achieves similar accuracy, the image modality and fusion machinery are not adding value, and budget should shift toward single-modality or different encoder choices. If RNA-only is substantially worse, it confirms the image modality contributes and justifies continued investment in multimodal configurations. This baseline is essential before spending further experiments on more complex multimodal variants, making it the highest-information-use next step under a limited budget."
}

